-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 22, CRIMINAL INTIMIDATION, INSULT AND
-- ANNOYANCE: ss 503-510.
--
--   s 503  defines "criminal intimidation"                  (the elements)
--   s 504  intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace
--   s 505  statements conducing to public mischief (with its own Exception)
--   s 506  punishes criminal intimidation, on two tiers
--   s 507  criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication
--   ss 508, 509, 510  repealed
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt), page footers removed.
--
-- Before reading:
--
-- * ss 503/506 follow the reference row's `criminal-intimidation-503-506.l4`
--   field for field and ladder for ladder, so the charge generator's
--   catalogue entry for s 506 (`Criminal Intimidation Facts`, `commits
--   criminal intimidation`, `offence under s 506`, `charge under s 506`) reads
--   this module unchanged. Two differences: the facts record has two more
--   leaves, for s 507; and the charge quotes the threat with straight quotes,
--   not curly ones, because notes/PLAN.md §1 makes the modules ASCII (FORK
--   DD-13 in notes/documents-defamation-forks.md).
-- * s 506 is ONE offence with TWO punishments (the reference row's reading):
--   the aggravated limb chooses the punishment, and is not on the offence
--   ladder. Both punishments are declared as data.
-- * Every other group's word these ladders read (grievous hurt, s 320; an
--   offence against the State, Chapter 6; against the public tranquillity,
--   Chapter 8; s 140B) is a flat BOOLEAN leaf whose @desc names its owner.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-common`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 22, criminal intimidation, insult and annoyance`

§§ `The facts of one threat - ss 503, 506, 507`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 503, 506, 507 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Criminal Intimidation Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim                IS A STRING  @desc The name of the person threatened, as it is to appear in the charge - for example "SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee"
    `victim described as` IS A STRING  @desc How the charge describes the person threatened, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `victim pronoun`      IS A Pronoun @desc The pronoun the charge uses for the person threatened
    `threat words`        IS A STRING  @desc The words of the threat, verbatim, as they are to be quoted after "by uttering" - for example "I will shoot her to death"; leave blank if the threat was not spoken
    language              IS A STRING  @desc The language the threat was uttered in - for example "Hokkien"; leave blank if it does not need stating

    -- s 503 "Whoever threatens another"
    `threatened the victim`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused threaten the person named? A threat may be made by words, in writing or by conduct. (Physical element, s 22A.)

    -- "with any injury to his person, reputation or property"
    person                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the threat threaten injury to the body of the person threatened - for example a threat to kill, to shoot or to beat?
    reputation            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the threat threaten injury to the reputation of the person threatened - for example a threat to publish something defamatory of them?
    property              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the threat threaten injury to the property of the person threatened - for example a threat to burn their house?

    -- "or to the person or reputation of any one in whom that person is interested"
    `person of one in whom interested`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the threat threaten injury to the body of somebody else the person threatened is interested in - for example their child?
    `reputation of one in whom interested`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the threat threaten injury to the reputation of somebody else the person threatened is interested in? The Explanation to s 503 puts a threat to injure the reputation of a DECEASED person they are interested in within the section.

    -- "with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to
    --  do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any
    --  act which that person is legally entitled to do, as the means of
    --  avoiding the execution of such threat"
    `cause alarm`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make the threat intending to cause alarm to the person threatened? Alarm the person in fact felt is evidence of this intent and is not the same thing as it. (Fault element, s 22A.)
    `do an act not legally bound to do`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the threat to make the person threatened do something they were under no legal duty to do ("legally bound to do", s 43)? (Fault element.)
    `omit an act legally entitled to do`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the threat to make the person threatened leave undone something they were legally entitled to do? (Fault element.)

    -- s 506, the aggravated limb: what the threat was a threat OF
    death                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat a threat to cause death?
    `grievous hurt`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat a threat to cause grievous hurt within section 320 - for example emasculation, loss of sight or hearing, or a fracture or dislocation of a bone? (s 320 is defined in pc-body-a; joined at integration)
    `the destruction of any property by fire`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat a threat to destroy any property by fire?
    `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or more`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat a threat to cause an offence punishable with death, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more?

    -- s 507
    `by an anonymous communication`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the criminal intimidation committed by an anonymous communication - a letter, message or call that did not say who it came from? (s 507)
    `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused take precautions to conceal the name or the abode of the person from whom the threat came - for example a false name, a borrowed phone or a disguised voice? (s 507)

§§ `s 503 - criminal intimidation`

-- 503. Whoever threatens another with any injury to his person, reputation or
--      property, or to the person or reputation of any one in whom that person
--      is interested, with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause
--      that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to
--      omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do, as the
--      means of avoiding the execution of such threat, commits criminal
--      intimidation.
--      Explanation.-A threat to injure the reputation of any deceased person
--      in whom the person threatened is interested, is within this section.
--      Illustration: A, for the purpose of inducing B to desist from
--      prosecuting a civil suit, threatens to burn B's house. A is guilty of
--      criminal intimidation.
--
-- "as the means of avoiding the execution of such threat" qualifies the two
-- inducement intents and not the alarm intent (FORK DD-12, the reference
-- row's call).
@export Whether the accused "commits criminal intimidation" within section 503 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat, what injury it threatened, and what the accused meant it to achieve
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits criminal intimidation` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `threatened the victim`
   ...  "with any injury to"
   ...  (        (    "his"
                 ...  (    f's person
                      ..   f's reputation
                      OR   f's property ) )
            OR   (    "or to the"
                 ...  (    f's `person of one in whom interested`
                      OR   f's `reputation of one in whom interested` ) ) )
   ...  "with intent to"
   ...  (        (    f's `cause alarm`
                 ...  "to that person" )
            OR   (    "or to cause that person to"
                 ...  (    f's `do an act not legally bound to do`
                      OR   f's `omit an act legally entitled to do` )
                 ...  "as the means of avoiding the execution of such threat" ) )

§§ `s 504 - intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace`

-- 504. Whoever intentionally insults, and thereby gives provocation to any
--      person, intending or knowing it to be likely that such provocation will
--      cause him to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      2 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 504 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Intentional Insult Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim                IS A STRING  @desc The name of the person insulted, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING  @desc How the charge describes the person insulted, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `victim pronoun`      IS A Pronoun @desc The pronoun the charge uses for the person insulted
    `the insult`          IS A STRING  @desc How the accused insulted the person, as it is to read after "by" - for example "uttering the words 'you are a thief' at him"
    `intentionally insults`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused insult the person intentionally (s 26C)? (Fault element and physical element together.)
    `thereby gives provocation to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the insult thereby give provocation to the person? (Physical element.)
    `intending that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the provocation to cause the person to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence (s 40)? (Fault element.)
    `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be likely that the provocation would cause the person to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence? (Fault element; s 26D.)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 504 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace)
GIVEN f IS AN `Intentional Insult Facts` @desc The insult, and what the accused meant or knew it would provoke
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 504` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `intentionally insults`
   ...  "and"
   ...  f's `thereby gives provocation to any person`
   ...  (    f's `intending that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`
        OR   f's `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 504
`punishment prescribed by s 504` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "504"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both" 24

§§ `s 505 - statements conducing to public mischief`

-- 505. Whoever makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report
--      in written, electronic or other media -
--      (a) with intent to cause, or which is likely to cause any officer or
--          serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces
--          lawfully present in Singapore, or any person to whom section 140B
--          refers, to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty as
--          such;
--      (b) with intent to cause, or which is likely to cause, fear or alarm to
--          the public, or to any section of the public, whereby any person may
--          be induced to commit an offence against the State or against the
--          public tranquillity; or
--      (c) with intent to incite, or which is likely to incite, any class or
--          community of persons to commit any offence against any other class
--          or community of persons,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      3 years, or with fine, or with both.
--      Exception.-It does not amount to an offence within the meaning of this
--      section, when the person making, publishing or circulating any such
--      statement, rumour or report ... has reasonable grounds for believing
--      that such statement, rumour or report is true and makes, publishes or
--      circulates it without any such intent as aforesaid.
--
-- The Exception is part of the section (notes/PLAN.md §5), so it is on the
-- ladder. It can only ever rescue a "likely to" limb: it requires the
-- statement to have been made "without any such intent" (FORK DD-11).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 505 - the operative atoms, the Exception, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Public Mischief Statement Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the statement`       IS A STRING  @desc The statement, rumour or report, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "a post on Facebook stating that ..."
    `makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make, publish or circulate a statement, rumour or report, in written, electronic or other media? (Physical element.)
    -- (a)
    `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused intend it to cause an officer or serviceman of the Singapore Armed Forces, of visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore, or a person s 140B refers to (defined in pc-state-public), to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty?
    `likely to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Was it likely to cause such an officer, serviceman or person to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty?
    -- (b)
    `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused intend it to cause fear or alarm to the public or a section of it, whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State (Chapter 6, pc-state-public) or against the public tranquillity (Chapter 8, pc-state-public)?
    `likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Was it likely to cause such fear or alarm, whereby any person may be so induced?
    -- (c)
    `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused intend it to incite a class or community of persons to commit an offence against another class or community?
    `likely to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Was it likely to incite a class or community of persons to commit an offence against another class or community?
    -- the Exception
    `has reasonable grounds for believing that the statement, rumour or report is true`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have reasonable grounds for believing the statement, rumour or report to be true? (Exception to s 505)

@export Whether one of the intents in paragraphs (a) to (c) of section 505 of the Penal Code 1871 is present ("any such intent as aforesaid")
GIVEN f IS A `Public Mischief Statement Facts` @desc The statement, and what the accused intended by it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `with any intent mentioned in section 505` f IF
        f's `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`
   OR   f's `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`
   OR   f's `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`

@export Whether the Exception to section 505 of the Penal Code 1871 applies
GIVEN f IS A `Public Mischief Statement Facts` @desc The statement, what the accused intended by it, and why he believed it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Exception to s 505 applies` f IF
        "Exception.-It does not amount to an offence ... when the person ..."
   AND  f's `has reasonable grounds for believing that the statement, rumour or report is true`
   AND  "and makes, publishes or circulates it without any such intent as aforesaid"
   AND  NOT `with any intent mentioned in section 505` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 505 of the Penal Code 1871 (statements conducing to public mischief)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Mischief Statement Facts` @desc The statement, what it was intended or likely to cause, and the accused's grounds for believing it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 505` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report`
   ...  "in written, electronic or other media -"
   ...  (    "(a)"
             ...  (    f's `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`
                  OR   f's `likely to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty` )
        OR   "(b)"
             ...  (    f's `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`
                  OR   f's `likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity` )
        OR   "(c)"
             ...  (    f's `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`
                  OR   f's `likely to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community` ) )
   ...  "Exception.-"
   ...  NOT `the Exception to s 505 applies` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 505
`punishment prescribed by s 505` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "505"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both" 36

§§ `s 506 - punishment for criminal intimidation`

-- 506. Whoever commits the offence of criminal intimidation shall be punished
--      with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine,
--      or with both; and if the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt, or
--      to cause the destruction of any property by fire, or to cause an
--      offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 7 years or more, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
-- One offence, two punishments. The offence ladder is s 503's, unchanged.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal intimidation)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat, what injury it threatened, and what the accused meant it to achieve
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 506` f IF
        "Whoever commits the offence of"
   ...  `commits criminal intimidation` f

-- The second half of s 506, which selects the punishment and proves nothing.
@export Whether the threat falls within the second limb of section 506 of the Penal Code 1871 (death, grievous hurt, fire, or a serious offence), which selects the higher punishment
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc What the threat was a threat of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` f IF
        "and if the threat is to cause"
   ..   f's death
   ..   f's `grievous hurt`
   ..   "or to cause" ... f's `the destruction of any property by fire`
   OR   "or to cause" ... f's `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or more`

-- The threshold in the second limb, as a helper over the threatened offence's
-- punishment (notes/PLAN.md §3.5): the ladder reads the BOOLEAN leaf
-- `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or more`,
-- and a fixture can set it from this. "which may extend to 7 years or more"
-- is read with s 41 (a maximum of exactly 7 years counts); a punishment that
-- prescribes imprisonment with no stated maximum is refused by s 41's own
-- helper in pc-general.
@export Whether an offence is "punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more" (s 506 of the Penal Code 1871, read with s 41)
GIVEN p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment the threatened offence's section prescribes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` p IF
        `prescribed at all` (p's death)
   OR   `punishable with imprisonment for` 84 `months or upwards within section 41` p

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 506, first limb
`punishment prescribed by s 506` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "506"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both" 24

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 506, second limb - "if the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt, or ... by fire, or ... an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for ... 7 years or more"
`punishment prescribed by s 506, where the threat is to cause death, grievous hurt, destruction by fire or a serious offence` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "506"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both" 120

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment under s 506` f MEANS
    IF   `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` f
    THEN `punishment prescribed by s 506, where the threat is to cause death, grievous hurt, destruction by fire or a serious offence`
    ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 506`

§§ `s 507 - criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication`

-- 507. Whoever commits the offence of criminal intimidation by an anonymous
--      communication, or by having taken precautions to conceal the name or
--      abode of the person from whom the threat comes, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, in addition to the
--      punishment provided for the offence by section 506.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 507 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat, how it was communicated, and what the accused meant it to achieve
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 507` f IF
        "Whoever commits the offence of"
   ...  `commits criminal intimidation` f
   ...  (    f's `by an anonymous communication`
        OR   f's `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes` )

-- "shall be punished with imprisonment ... in addition to the punishment
-- provided ... by section 506": imprisonment is mandatory here (FORK DD-14).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 507
`punishment prescribed by s 507` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        section                  IS "507"
        words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, in addition to the punishment provided for the offence by section 506"
        death                    IS `not prescribed`
        `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
        imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
        `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
        `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
        `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
        fine                     IS `not prescribed`
        `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
        `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
        caning                   IS `not prescribed`
        `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- s 508. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 509. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 510. [Repealed by Act 5 of 2015]

§ `The charges - Chapter 22`

§§ `Criminal intimidation - ss 506, 507`

-- CPC s 125 requires the manner for criminal intimidation. Chan Yok Tuang v PP
-- [2008] SGHC 137:
--   did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the
--   person of SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee; to wit, by uttering "I will shoot
--   her to death" in Hokkien at her, with intent to cause alarm to the said
--   SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the intimidation` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to ", (`the injuries threatened` f),
           (`the utterance clause` f),
           ", with intent to ", (`the intents` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the injuries threatened` f MEANS
    `joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's person) ("the person of " APPEND `the person threatened` f)),
        (`included if` (f's reputation) ("the reputation of " APPEND `the person threatened` f)),
        (`included if` (f's property) ("the property of " APPEND `the person threatened` f)),
        (`included if` (f's `person of one in whom interested`) (CONCAT "the person of one in whom the said ", f's victim, " is interested")),
        (`included if` (f's `reputation of one in whom interested`) (CONCAT "the reputation of one in whom the said ", f's victim, " is interested"))))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the person threatened` f MEANS
    IF   f's `victim described as` EQUALS ""
    THEN f's victim
    ELSE CONCAT f's victim, ", ", f's `victim described as`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the utterance clause` f MEANS
    IF   f's `threat words` EQUALS ""
    THEN ""
    ELSE CONCAT "; to wit, by uttering \"", f's `threat words`, "\"", (`the language clause` f), " at ", (`object pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the language clause` f MEANS
    IF   f's language EQUALS ""
    THEN ""
    ELSE " in " APPEND f's language

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the intents` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and to " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `cause alarm`) ("cause alarm to the said " APPEND f's victim)),
        (`included if` (f's `do an act not legally bound to do`)
            (CONCAT "cause the said ", f's victim, " to do an act which ", (`subject pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " is not legally bound to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of the said threat")),
        (`included if` (f's `omit an act legally entitled to do`)
            (CONCAT "cause the said ", f's victim, " to omit to do an act which ", (`subject pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of the said threat"))))

-- s 507's manner: the intimidation, and how it was made anonymous.
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the anonymity clause` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `by an anonymous communication`) "by an anonymous communication"),
        (`included if` (f's `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes`) "by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat came")))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of criminal intimidation not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `threatened the victim`) "threatens another"),
        (`missing unless` (f's person OR f's reputation OR f's property OR f's `person of one in whom interested` OR f's `reputation of one in whom interested`) "with any injury to his person, reputation or property, or to the person or reputation of any one in whom that person is interested"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `cause alarm` OR f's `do an act not legally bound to do` OR f's `omit an act legally entitled to do`) "with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits criminal intimidation` f) "the elements of section 503 taken together"))

@export Frame a charge under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal intimidation), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat, what it threatened, what it was meant to achieve, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 506` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "506" "criminal intimidation"
        ((`the punishment under s 506` f)'s words)
        (`offence under s 506` f)
        (`the manner of the intimidation` f)
        (`elements of criminal intimidation not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 507 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat, how it was communicated, what it was meant to achieve, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 507` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "507" "criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 507`'s words)
        (`offence under s 507` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the intimidation` f), ", ", (`the anonymity clause` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of criminal intimidation not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `by an anonymous communication` OR f's `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes`)
                          "by an anonymous communication, or by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes")))

§§ `Intentional insult - s 504`

GIVEN f IS AN `Intentional Insult Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the insult` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did intentionally insult ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
           " by ", f's `the insult`,
           ", and thereby gave provocation to the said ", f's victim, ", ",
           (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
               (`included if` (f's `intending that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`) "intending"),
               (`included if` (f's `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`) "knowing it to be likely")))),
           " that such provocation would cause ", (`object pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence"

@export Frame a charge under section 504 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Intentional Insult Facts` @desc The insult, what it was meant or known to provoke, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 504` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "504" "intentional insult with intent to provoke a breach of the peace"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 504`'s words)
        (`offence under s 504` f)
        (`the manner of the insult` f)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `intentionally insults`) "intentionally insults"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `thereby gives provocation to any person`) "and thereby gives provocation to any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence`)
                "intending or knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence")))

§§ `Statements conducing to public mischief - s 505`

GIVEN f IS A `Public Mischief Statement Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the statement` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did make, publish or circulate a statement, to wit, ", f's `the statement`, ", ",
           `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
               (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`) "with intent to cause any officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty as such"),
               (`included if` (f's `likely to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`) "which was likely to cause any officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty as such"),
               (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`) "with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public, whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or against the public tranquillity"),
               (`included if` (f's `likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`) "which was likely to cause fear or alarm to the public, whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or against the public tranquillity"),
               (`included if` (f's `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`) "with intent to incite a class or community of persons to commit an offence against another class or community of persons"),
               (`included if` (f's `likely to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`) "which was likely to incite a class or community of persons to commit an offence against another class or community of persons")))

@export Frame a charge under section 505 of the Penal Code 1871 (statements conducing to public mischief), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Mischief Statement Facts` @desc The statement, what it was intended or likely to cause, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 505` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "505" "statements conducing to public mischief"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 505`'s words)
        (`offence under s 505` f)
        (`the manner of the statement` f)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report`) "makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty` OR f's `likely to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty`
                               OR f's `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity` OR f's `likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity`
                               OR f's `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community` OR f's `likely to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community`)
                "with an intent in, or likely to cause an effect in, paragraph (a), (b) or (c)"),
            (`missing unless` (NOT `the Exception to s 505 applies` f) "not within the Exception (reasonable grounds for believing the statement true, and no such intent)")))
